        "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{80}{4} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
